  "security_implications": "encode_keylen[0] is part of the key-initialization prefix for KMAC. If key_len_i takes an unsupported value, encode_keylen[0] = 0 is used, which might skip or weaken key absorption. An error in the encoded constants (width truncation or wrong swap) could systematically corrupt the key schedule, leading to incorrect MAC output or potential forgeries. Parameter MaxEncodedKeyLenSize must be verified to prevent silent truncation.",
